# Mesa 26.2.6 (llvmpipe behind GLFW's EGL/Wayland path) keeps two one-time
# caches in libgallium: get_cpu_topology() allocates the CPU topology mask
# during eglInitialize(), and u_mmInit() allocates the JIT allocator state
# on the first glDrawArrays(). GLFW's glfwTerminate() dlclose()s libEGL and
# libgallium, so LSan loses the owning globals and reports these still-live
# blocks as leaks. No Lumina allocation is involved; all RHI RAII wrappers
# release their objects before the window is destroyed.
#
# The allocation stacks are only symbolized through the surviving GLFW frame
# (_glfwInitEGL) and the Lumina call site (FRHICommandList::Draw). Mesa's own
# frames are in unloaded modules and cannot be matched by LSan.
leak:_glfwInitEGL
leak:FRHICommandList::Draw
